{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY"},{"type":"text","value":" summarizes raw observations into vertical boxplots. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX"},{"type":"text","value":" transposes\nthe same statistical and interaction semantics into horizontal boxplots.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxRows"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes their eager semantic preparation for reuse outside a mark."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { boxY } from '@tanstack/charts/box'\n\nboxY(rows, {\n  x: 'group',\n  y: 'value',\n  key: 'id',\n  fill: '#bfdbfe',\n  stroke: '#2563eb',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The transform and both marks are also exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/universal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"signatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function boxY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction boxX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n\nfunction boxRows<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxRowsOptions<TDatum>,\n): BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredCategory>[]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY"},{"type":"text","value":" requires a categorical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" channel and numeric "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" channel. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrequires numeric "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" and categorical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary-semantics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary semantics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For each non-null category, the mark:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"keeps finite numeric observations;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"computes linearly interpolated first quartile, median, and third quartile;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"places Tukey fences at 1.5 times the interquartile range below and above\nthe box;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"uses the lowest and highest observed values inside those fences as\nwhiskers; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"emits observations strictly outside the fences as outliers."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categories retain first-seen order. Outliers retain their global source order,\nincluding when category rows are interleaved. A category with no finite value\nis omitted. Singleton, two-value, and zero-IQR groups use the same rules rather\nthan a separate fallback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mark composes a whisker link, interquartile bar, median tick, and outlier\ndots. Those native children remain renderer-neutral; the mark does not emit a\ncustom SVG path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"eager-rows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eager rows"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxRows"},{"type":"text","value":" when the same summary feeds multiple marks, a table, or\napplication logic:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { boxRows } from '@tanstack/charts/box'\n\nconst prepared = boxRows(rows, {\n  category: 'group',\n  value: 'measurement',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"category"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" use the standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue"},{"type":"text","value":" contract. A field\nname reads that field. An accessor receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ datum, index, data }"},{"type":"text","value":".\nPreparation is eager, does not mutate source rows, and returns all summary rows\nfollowed by outliers in global source order. The result contains semantic data\nand lineage only; child-mark identity remains internal to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable parent mark ID"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY: Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX: Channel<TDatum, number?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY"},{"type":"text","value":"; finite observation for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY: Channel<TDatum, number?>"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX: Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finite observation for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxY"},{"type":"text","value":"; category for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boxX"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable raw-observation identity, including duplicate outliers"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#ccc"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interquartile box fill"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fillOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interquartile box fill opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"currentColor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whisker, median, and outlier stroke"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeOpacity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whisker, median, and outlier stroke opacity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per child"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overrides whisker, median, and outlier widths together"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pixels removed from both categorical edges of box and median"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"r"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outlier radius in pixels"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMotionDefinition<BoxDatum<...>>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion for derived summary and outlier data"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The orientation determines the exact "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" channel types; the combined\nrow above is shorthand. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" when naming an\noptions object separately."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"derived-data-and-lineage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Derived data and lineage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The chart datum is a discriminated union:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type BoxDatum<TDatum, TCategory> =\n  | {\n      kind: 'summary'\n      category: TCategory\n      q1: number\n      median: number\n      q3: number\n      whiskerLow: number\n      whiskerHigh: number\n      count: number\n      source: readonly TDatum[]\n      sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n    }\n  | {\n      kind: 'outlier'\n      category: TCategory\n      value: number\n      source: readonly [TDatum]\n      sourceIndexes: readonly [number]\n    }","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"datum.kind"},{"type":"text","value":" in tooltip, motion, or selection code. Summary lineage contains\nevery finite contributing observation in source order. An outlier retains its\nexact source row and index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public type surface includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxDatum"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxYDatum"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxXDatum"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxSummaryDatum"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxOutlierDatum"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxRowsOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxYOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BoxXOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each category contributes one summary point owned by the box body and anchored\nat the median. The whisker and median tick are decorative. Each outlier dot\ncontributes its own point and raw-row lineage. This keeps pointer, keyboard,\ntooltip, and motion behavior from receiving duplicate summary targets for the\nsame category."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" when observation identity matters across updates or when duplicate\noutlier values can occur in one category."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"signatures","text":"Signatures","level":2},{"id":"summary-semantics","text":"Summary semantics","level":2},{"id":"eager-rows","text":"Eager rows","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"derived-data-and-lineage","text":"Derived data and lineage","level":2},{"id":"interaction","text":"Interaction","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`boxY` summarizes raw observations into vertical boxplots. `boxX` transposes\nthe same statistical and interaction semantics into horizontal boxplots.\n`boxRows` exposes their eager semantic preparation for reuse outside a mark.\n\n```ts\nimport { boxY } from '@tanstack/charts/box'\n\nboxY(rows, {\n  x: 'group',\n  y: 'value',\n  key: 'id',\n  fill: '#bfdbfe',\n  stroke: '#2563eb',\n})\n```\n\nThe transform and both marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction boxY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction boxX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n\nfunction boxRows<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxRowsOptions<TDatum>,\n): BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredCategory>[]\n```\n\n`boxY` requires a categorical `x` channel and numeric `y` channel. `boxX`\nrequires numeric `x` and categorical `y`.\n\n## Summary semantics\n\nFor each non-null category, the mark:\n\n1. keeps finite numeric observations;\n2. computes linearly interpolated first quartile, median, and third quartile;\n3. places Tukey fences at 1.5 times the interquartile range below and above\n   the box;\n4. uses the lowest and highest observed values inside those fences as\n   whiskers; and\n5. emits observations strictly outside the fences as outliers.\n\nCategories retain first-seen order. Outliers retain their global source order,\nincluding when category rows are interleaved. A category with no finite value\nis omitted. Singleton, two-value, and zero-IQR groups use the same rules rather\nthan a separate fallback.\n\nThe mark composes a whisker link, interquartile bar, median tick, and outlier\ndots. Those native children remain renderer-neutral; the mark does not emit a\ncustom SVG path.\n\n## Eager rows\n\nUse `boxRows` when the same summary feeds multiple marks, a table, or\napplication logic:\n\n```ts\nimport { boxRows } from '@tanstack/charts/box'\n\nconst prepared = boxRows(rows, {\n  category: 'group',\n  value: 'measurement',\n})\n```\n\n`category` and `value` use the standard `TransformValue` contract. A field\nname reads that field. An accessor receives `{ datum, index, data }`.\nPreparation is eager, does not mutate source rows, and returns all summary rows\nfollowed by outliers in global source order. The result contains semantic data\nand lineage only; child-mark identity remains internal to `boxX` and `boxY`.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option          | Type                                                                   | Default        | Meaning                                                       |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`            | `string`                                                               | Layer-derived  | Stable parent mark ID                                         |\n| `x`             | `boxY: Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`; `boxX: Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Required       | Category for `boxY`; finite observation for `boxX`            |\n| `y`             | `boxY: Channel<TDatum, number?>`; `boxX: Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>` | Required       | Finite observation for `boxY`; category for `boxX`            |\n| `key`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                                            | Inferred       | Stable raw-observation identity, including duplicate outliers |\n| `fill`          | `string`                                                               | `#ccc`         | Interquartile box fill                                        |\n| `fillOpacity`   | `number`                                                               | SVG default    | Interquartile box fill opacity                                |\n| `stroke`        | `string`                                                               | `currentColor` | Whisker, median, and outlier stroke                           |\n| `strokeOpacity` | `number`                                                               | SVG default    | Whisker, median, and outlier stroke opacity                   |\n| `strokeWidth`   | `number`                                                               | Per child      | Overrides whisker, median, and outlier widths together        |\n| `inset`         | `number`                                                               | `0`            | Pixels removed from both categorical edges of box and median  |\n| `r`             | `number`                                                               | `3`            | Outlier radius in pixels                                      |\n| `motion`        | `ChartMotionDefinition<BoxDatum<...>>`                                 | None           | Motion for derived summary and outlier data                   |\n\nThe orientation determines the exact `x` and `y` channel types; the combined\nrow above is shorthand. Use `BoxYOptions` or `BoxXOptions` when naming an\noptions object separately.\n\n## Derived data and lineage\n\nThe chart datum is a discriminated union:\n\n```ts\ntype BoxDatum<TDatum, TCategory> =\n  | {\n      kind: 'summary'\n      category: TCategory\n      q1: number\n      median: number\n      q3: number\n      whiskerLow: number\n      whiskerHigh: number\n      count: number\n      source: readonly TDatum[]\n      sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n    }\n  | {\n      kind: 'outlier'\n      category: TCategory\n      value: number\n      source: readonly [TDatum]\n      sourceIndexes: readonly [number]\n    }\n```\n\nUse `datum.kind` in tooltip, motion, or selection code. Summary lineage contains\nevery finite contributing observation in source order. An outlier retains its\nexact source row and index.\n\nThe public type surface includes `BoxDatum`, `BoxYDatum`, `BoxXDatum`,\n`BoxSummaryDatum`, `BoxOutlierDatum`, `BoxRowsOptions`, `BoxYOptions`, and\n`BoxXOptions`.\n\n## Interaction\n\nEach category contributes one summary point owned by the box body and anchored\nat the median. The whisker and median tick are decorative. Each outlier dot\ncontributes its own point and raw-row lineage. This keeps pointer, keyboard,\ntooltip, and motion behavior from receiving duplicate summary targets for the\nsame category.\n\nSupply `key` when observation identity matters across updates or when duplicate\noutlier values can occur in one category.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Box Marks\ndescription: Reference for boxRows, boxY, and boxX Tukey summaries, quartiles, whiskers, outliers, lineage, styling, and interaction.\n---\n\n`boxY` summarizes raw observations into vertical boxplots. `boxX` transposes\nthe same statistical and interaction semantics into horizontal boxplots.\n`boxRows` exposes their eager semantic preparation for reuse outside a mark.\n\n```ts\nimport { boxY } from '@tanstack/charts/box'\n\nboxY(rows, {\n  x: 'group',\n  y: 'value',\n  key: 'id',\n  fill: '#bfdbfe',\n  stroke: '#2563eb',\n})\n```\n\nThe transform and both marks are also exported from `@tanstack/charts` and\n`@tanstack/charts/universal`.\n\n## Signatures\n\n```ts\nfunction boxY<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxYOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredX>, InferredX, number>\n\nfunction boxX<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxXOptions<TDatum>,\n): ChartMark<BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredY>, number, InferredY>\n\nfunction boxRows<TDatum>(\n  source: Iterable<TDatum>,\n  options: BoxRowsOptions<TDatum>,\n): BoxDatum<TDatum, InferredCategory>[]\n```\n\n`boxY` requires a categorical `x` channel and numeric `y` channel. `boxX`\nrequires numeric `x` and categorical `y`.\n\n## Summary semantics\n\nFor each non-null category, the mark:\n\n1. keeps finite numeric observations;\n2. computes linearly interpolated first quartile, median, and third quartile;\n3. places Tukey fences at 1.5 times the interquartile range below and above\n   the box;\n4. uses the lowest and highest observed values inside those fences as\n   whiskers; and\n5. emits observations strictly outside the fences as outliers.\n\nCategories retain first-seen order. Outliers retain their global source order,\nincluding when category rows are interleaved. A category with no finite value\nis omitted. Singleton, two-value, and zero-IQR groups use the same rules rather\nthan a separate fallback.\n\nThe mark composes a whisker link, interquartile bar, median tick, and outlier\ndots. Those native children remain renderer-neutral; the mark does not emit a\ncustom SVG path.\n\n## Eager rows\n\nUse `boxRows` when the same summary feeds multiple marks, a table, or\napplication logic:\n\n```ts\nimport { boxRows } from '@tanstack/charts/box'\n\nconst prepared = boxRows(rows, {\n  category: 'group',\n  value: 'measurement',\n})\n```\n\n`category` and `value` use the standard `TransformValue` contract. A field\nname reads that field. An accessor receives `{ datum, index, data }`.\nPreparation is eager, does not mutate source rows, and returns all summary rows\nfollowed by outliers in global source order. The result contains semantic data\nand lineage only; child-mark identity remains internal to `boxX` and `boxY`.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option          | Type                                                                   | Default        | Meaning                                                       |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id`            | `string`                                                               | Layer-derived  | Stable parent mark ID                                         |\n| `x`             | `boxY: Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>`; `boxX: Channel<TDatum, number?>` | Required       | Category for `boxY`; finite observation for `boxX`            |\n| `y`             | `boxY: Channel<TDatum, number?>`; `boxX: Channel<TDatum, ChartValue?>` | Required       | Finite observation for `boxY`; category for `boxX`            |\n| `key`           | `Channel<TDatum, ChartKey>`                                            | Inferred       | Stable raw-observation identity, including duplicate outliers |\n| `fill`          | `string`                                                               | `#ccc`         | Interquartile box fill                                        |\n| `fillOpacity`   | `number`                                                               | SVG default    | Interquartile box fill opacity                                |\n| `stroke`        | `string`                                                               | `currentColor` | Whisker, median, and outlier stroke                           |\n| `strokeOpacity` | `number`                                                               | SVG default    | Whisker, median, and outlier stroke opacity                   |\n| `strokeWidth`   | `number`                                                               | Per child      | Overrides whisker, median, and outlier widths together        |\n| `inset`         | `number`                                                               | `0`            | Pixels removed from both categorical edges of box and median  |\n| `r`             | `number`                                                               | `3`            | Outlier radius in pixels                                      |\n| `motion`        | `ChartMotionDefinition<BoxDatum<...>>`                                 | None           | Motion for derived summary and outlier data                   |\n\nThe orientation determines the exact `x` and `y` channel types; the combined\nrow above is shorthand. Use `BoxYOptions` or `BoxXOptions` when naming an\noptions object separately.\n\n## Derived data and lineage\n\nThe chart datum is a discriminated union:\n\n```ts\ntype BoxDatum<TDatum, TCategory> =\n  | {\n      kind: 'summary'\n      category: TCategory\n      q1: number\n      median: number\n      q3: number\n      whiskerLow: number\n      whiskerHigh: number\n      count: number\n      source: readonly TDatum[]\n      sourceIndexes: readonly number[]\n    }\n  | {\n      kind: 'outlier'\n      category: TCategory\n      value: number\n      source: readonly [TDatum]\n      sourceIndexes: readonly [number]\n    }\n```\n\nUse `datum.kind` in tooltip, motion, or selection code. Summary lineage contains\nevery finite contributing observation in source order. An outlier retains its\nexact source row and index.\n\nThe public type surface includes `BoxDatum`, `BoxYDatum`, `BoxXDatum`,\n`BoxSummaryDatum`, `BoxOutlierDatum`, `BoxRowsOptions`, `BoxYOptions`, and\n`BoxXOptions`.\n\n## Interaction\n\nEach category contributes one summary point owned by the box body and anchored\nat the median. The whisker and median tick are decorative. Each outlier dot\ncontributes its own point and raw-row lineage. This keeps pointer, keyboard,\ntooltip, and motion behavior from receiving duplicate summary targets for the\nsame category.\n\nSupply `key` when observation identity matters across updates or when duplicate\noutlier values can occur in one category.\n"}
